WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
Varys: Aegon landed at the mouth of&nbsp;
the Blackwater River and raised a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:08.800
primitive Aegonfort in the disputed lands&nbsp;
between Harren's and Argilac's kingdom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:15.280
so that neither could decide whose problem he was.&nbsp;
Adopting the customs of the Seven Kingdoms, Aegon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:20.160
unfurled his own banner with a red three-headed&nbsp;
dragon breathing fire upon a black field.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:27.200
Visenya crowned him with a ruby-studded circlet&nbsp;
of Valyrian steel while Rhaenys hailed him as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:33.360
the first high king the continent had seen since&nbsp;
the Dawn Age. As his lords and the gathered locals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:39.840
cheered him, Aegon named his loyal friends&nbsp;
to a small council led by Orys Baratheon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:47.120
whom he called "my strong right hand." The title&nbsp;
stuck, and he became the first Hand of the King.
&nbsp;

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:53.360
But for now, Aegon's kingdom contained only&nbsp;
a rocky island and a handful of fields.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.080
The other kings had large armies, ships, castles,&nbsp;
and thousands of years of rule. But Aegon had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:07.120
dragons. He had chosen for the words of his&nbsp;
house, "Fire and Blood." Before he was done,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:13.600
the rivers, fields, and skies would turn red.
Viserys Targaryen: Soon after his coronation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:19.680
Aegon returned to the mouth of the Blackwater&nbsp;
River, where he had first set foot on Westeros.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:26.960
A small town had since sprouted around his&nbsp;
primitive fort. To honor their new master,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:32.080
the locals dubbed it "King's Landing,"&nbsp;
though it looked more fit for a hedge knight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:38.160
with wooden palisades, muddy streets,&nbsp;
and piles of mangled swords carted in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.800
from every corner of the conquest.
But when Aegon made it his court,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:50.800
wood became stone, black mud was buried beneath a&nbsp;
Red Keep, and the collected swords of Aegon's foes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:57.680
were blasted by dragon fire and became a seat&nbsp;
fit for the Conqueror and the greatest dynasty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:05.600
this world has ever known. House Targaryen. 
Varys: King's Landing is both a city and a curse.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:11.520
Aegon the Conqueror was the first king&nbsp;
to land there. His first conquest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:15.280
a tiny village at the mouth of the Blackwater&nbsp;
River, where he raised a wooden fort.
&nbsp;

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.360
When it became clear that Aegon would earn his&nbsp;
title, people flocked to the fort and renamed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:27.440
it "King's Landing" in his honor. The ploy&nbsp;
succeeded, and Aegon chose King's Landing for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:33.600
his capital over older and more beautiful&nbsp;
cities like Oldtown and anywhere else.
&nbsp;

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:39.200
The currying of royal favor thus became&nbsp;
the foundation of the city, and blood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:44.560
its bricks. Maegor the Cruel, Aegon's&nbsp;
son, completed the city's famous Red&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:50.640
Keep to hold the trappings of power: the royal&nbsp;
family, the Kingsguard, and the Iron Throne.
&nbsp;

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:56.960
To maintain the new castle's secrets, Maegor&nbsp;
murdered all its masons and craftsmen at a feast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:04.160
which he catered with the new castle servants,&nbsp;
who soon found all its secrets for himself.
&nbsp;

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:08.800
When the Faith Militant challenged his rule,&nbsp;
Maegor razed their Sept of Remembrance to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:12.960
ground with them inside at prayer and&nbsp;
erected the Dragonpit on the ashes.
&nbsp;

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:17.840
Petyr Baelish: Prince Maegor, a&nbsp;
warrior who was proud and arrogant.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:23.520
Maegor agreed to marry the High Septon's&nbsp;
niece to unite the Faith and the Crown,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:30.160
but then secretly wed a second wife in a Valyrian&nbsp;
ceremony artfully combining bigamy and heresy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:35.920
When word of it got out, the King was forced to&nbsp;
exile Maegor and choose a septon as his new Hand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:42.880
But the damage had been done. The King had trusted&nbsp;
in family, and his brother had set off a rebellion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:47.600
that would claim his rule and his life.
The High Sparrow:When Aegon's heir wed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:52.880
his daughter to his son, the Faith&nbsp;
could brook such abomination no longer.
&nbsp;

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:58.560
The High Septon led the denunciation of&nbsp;
the Targaryens. And all over Westeros,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:03.040
the Faith Militant took up their swords&nbsp;
against the dynasty and its supporters.
&nbsp;

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:09.600
The Faith Militant set upon and punished&nbsp;
the septon who had performed the ceremony.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:16.000
A few of the Faith Militant's more militant&nbsp;
members even scaled the walls of the castle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:20.080
and would have slain the king and his&nbsp;
family, had a knight of the Kingsguard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:26.480
not intervened. Frightened, the king fled to&nbsp;
Dragonstone, where he soon died of cramps.
&nbsp;

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:34.880
And so ascended the king's younger brother, Maegor&nbsp;
the Cruel. His first act was to challenge the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:42.320
Faith Militant to kill him if they believed his&nbsp;
rule to be ungodly. To the order's eternal credit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:50.560
they accepted. Ser Damon Morrigen proposed a&nbsp;
"trial by seven," Ser Damon and six of the Faith&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:57.360
Militant against the king and his six champions.&nbsp;
It was a contest in which the kingdom itself was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:05.040
at stake, and the accounts and tales are many.
But at the end of it, Maegor alone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:12.320
lived, proving that the throne was rightfully&nbsp;
his. He mounted the black dragon, Balerion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:17.200
and burned down the sept in King's Landing&nbsp;
while the Faith Militant were inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:24.240
at morning prayers. The screams of the burning and&nbsp;
dying men were said to echo throughout the city.
&nbsp;

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:30.960
Though Maegor had won the trial by seven, he&nbsp;
demanded the complete destruction of the Faith&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:36.960
Militant and the Faith itself, if necessary. He&nbsp;
made war upon the order wherever he found it.
&nbsp;

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:44.000
Yet the Faith Militant would not surrender,&nbsp;
raising armies of their own and turning Maegor's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:52.080
own lords against him. The Father's justice&nbsp;
may not always be swift, but it is certain.
&nbsp;

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.880
One morning, Maegor was found&nbsp;
dead on the Iron Throne.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:04.480
No one knows how. Maegor's cruelty died with him.
His successor saw the wisdom of a united crown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:11.600
and faith, and his Hand reached an accord with the&nbsp;
High Septon. As long as the Iron Throne defended&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:18.240
the Faith, the Faith would put aside its own&nbsp;
swords and its condemnation of the Targaryens.
&nbsp;

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:41.600
Viserys Targaryen:The Dance began, as many&nbsp;
dances do, with an old man and a young girl.
&nbsp;

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:45.680
The queen had failed to produce a son for&nbsp;
her king, so he anointed his daughter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:48.960
the Princess Rhaenyra, as&nbsp;
his heir. But years later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:53.200
the king remarried, and his new wife,&nbsp;
Queen Alicent of House Hightower,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:58.240
gave him a son. Feeble and foolish, the&nbsp;
old king refused to change the succession.
&nbsp;

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:03.520
He didn't even see how his court had split&nbsp;
into two rival camps of Blacks and Greens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:06.800
after the dresses that the princess and&nbsp;
the queen had worn to some tourney.
&nbsp;

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:14.320
One night, a servant found the old king&nbsp;
had died in his sleep and ran to inform&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:20.080
Queen Alicent. Protocol dictated that the bells&nbsp;
would be rung and a raven sent to Dragonstone to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:25.440
summon the heir, Princess Rhaenyra, for her&nbsp;
coronation. But Alicent had other plans.
&nbsp;

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:30.240
None were more surprised to hear of Prince&nbsp;
Aegon's succession than Prince Aegon himself.
&nbsp;

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:35.360
At first, the fool rejected the crown, but his&nbsp;
mother pointed out that his sister Rhaenyra&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:39.920
would return such loyalty by taking his&nbsp;
head. As the old king's trueborn son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:44.560
he'd always be a threat. Aegon relented.
He was crowned in the Dragonpit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:49.920
and his wife and sister Helaena became queen. His&nbsp;
brother Aemond flew off to win over the few great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:54.640
lords whose support Aegon didn't already&nbsp;
have. The banner of the gold dragon flew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:59.520
over King's Landing and the Red Keep as Aegon,&nbsp;
Second of His Name, ascended the Iron Throne.
&nbsp;

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:04.080
He would not sit it long.
Robert Baratheon: One day King's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:10.720
Landing looked up and saw two dragons circling&nbsp;
their foul city. Daemon and Rhaenyra had come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:17.760
for her throne, for the city was defenseless.
Aemond had taken the king's army from the city,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:25.120
and worse, he'd taken his dragon Vhagar. Seeing&nbsp;
that resistance was hopeless, the small council&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:30.000
surrendered the city, the Queen Mother&nbsp;
Alicent, and the broken Queen Helaena.
&nbsp;

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:35.840
But not King Aegon.
Somehow, despite his wounds and delirium,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:41.360
he had vanished from the city.&nbsp;
And so Queen Rhaenyra climbed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:47.920
steps and seated herself of the Iron Throne.
Legend has it that as she left that hall later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:55.760
blood trickled down her legs and hands, proving&nbsp;
the Iron Throne had spurned her. Nonsense! It's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.760 --> 00:09:02.640
chair made of steel blades. Rhaenyra had wanted it&nbsp;
all her life and had sacrificed two sons for it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:08.640
She likely gripped the damn thing too tight.
Shireen Baratheon: When Rhaenyra's last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:12.400
son wed Aegon's only daughter, the&nbsp;
Dance of Dragons officially ended.
&nbsp;

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:17.680
Ash and burned men. All that&nbsp;
was left of the Riverlands.
&nbsp;

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:21.840
Two scared children spouting&nbsp;
oaths they didn't understand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:29.760
All that was left of the mighty House Targaryen.
Ancient skulls and hatchlings that grew no bigger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:35.680
than cats. All that was left of the dragons.
The High Sparrow: To steward his monument to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:41.600
vanity, Baelor summoned the High Septon of&nbsp;
the Faith from his ancient seat in Oldtown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:46.320
and gifted him with ornate robes&nbsp;
and a crown of crystal and gold.
&nbsp;

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:52.400
And like a fool, the High&nbsp;
Septon put on his lord's motley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:59.520
and danced at his lord's table, and with each&nbsp;
passing year, the High Septons fell ever lower.
&nbsp;

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:08.640
How can the flock be kept safe from wolves when&nbsp;
the shepherd sleeps in their den? Baelor himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:13.520
appointed a simple-minded stonemason,&nbsp;
believing him the Smith reborn.
&nbsp;

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:20.320
And when he died, Baelor replaced him with&nbsp;
an eight-year-old boy whom Baelor had seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:24.240
speaking with doves that answered&nbsp;
with the voices of the Seven.
&nbsp;

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:29.520
Still, the common people&nbsp;
revere Baelor as the Blessed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:33.680
They tell of how he forced a high&nbsp;
lord to wash a beggar's feet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:41.120
fasted to tame his unnatural lusts and walked&nbsp;
the Boneway himself to make peace with Dorne.
&nbsp;

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:47.840
Many septons and septas even claim that&nbsp;
Baelor rescued his cousin, the Dragonknight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:55.120
from a snake pit because no viper would&nbsp;
strike a man so pure and holy. A lie!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.240 --> 00:11:00.480
Baelor was bitten a dozen times&nbsp;
and was bedridden for half a year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:05.440
and yet he didn't die.
Petyr Baelish: When the last dragon died,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:09.280
it was only a matter of time&nbsp;
before the Targaryens followed.
&nbsp;

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:15.680
Varys: By "only," you mean another century?
Baelish: Which they wasted trying to replace&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:20.960
their lost advantage: incinerating&nbsp;
their own palaces to hatch dragon eggs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:27.520
drinking wildfire to become dragons, and, let's&nbsp;
not forget the Mad King's favorite, burning men&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:34.000
alive so he could pretend to be a dragon.
Jaime Lannister: Kingslayer. A word every man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:37.920
and woman in Westeros spits at me, though&nbsp;
many can't name the king I slayed.
&nbsp;

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:44.640
I understand. To them, I'm a symbol of everything&nbsp;
they'll never have and a warning that'll never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:50.960
apply. So they can loathe me from the safety&nbsp;
of their small lives. But when a dog goes mad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:55.440
we put it down. Why not a king?
I served at the king's pleasure as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.440 --> 00:12:01.120
he burned Rickard Stark alive and strangled&nbsp;
his son, inciting the rebellion. I defended&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:05.360
the king's honor against courtiers as his&nbsp;
generals lost battle after battle with Robert.
&nbsp;

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:11.600
I kept the king's secrets when his pyromancers&nbsp;
hid caches of wildfire beneath King's Landing.
&nbsp;

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:15.920
I gave the king counsel when my&nbsp;
father's army was at the city gate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:21.680
and Grand Maester Pycelle lied that my father&nbsp;
had come to save him. Many forget that I also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:25.360
tried to defend the king from harm.
When the Lannister soldiers poured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:29.040
through the gates, it fell to me to hold the&nbsp;
Red Keep as the only Kingsguard in the city.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:33.040
I knew we were lost and sent to Aerys,&nbsp;
asking his leave to make terms.
&nbsp;

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:39.600
My man came back with the royal command. "Bring&nbsp;
me your father's head if you are no traitor."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:44.880
Aerys would have no yielding. His&nbsp;
pyromancer was with him, my messenger said.
&nbsp;

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:51.680
I knew what that meant. Aerys Targaryen was alone&nbsp;
in his throne room when I found him, picking at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:56.480
his scabbed and bleeding hands. The fool was&nbsp;
always cutting himself on the Iron Throne.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.360 --> 00:13:02.720
"Burn them! Burn them!" he kept muttering.
Aerys had decided to let Robert be king,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:06.720
after all, over the charred bones&nbsp;
and ashes of King's Landing.
&nbsp;

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:11.200
He must have thought his pyromancer was near&nbsp;
enough to obey him, but I'd killed him a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:14.320
minutes before in the courtyard.
As I approached the throne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:19.120
sanity flashed behind the King's eyes for a&nbsp;
moment, just long enough to read the look in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:24.240
mine. His eyes grew huge, and the royal mouth&nbsp;
drooped open in shock. He turned and ran.
&nbsp;

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:31.120
A single thrust was all it took to end the&nbsp;
greatest dynasty the world had ever seen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:35.920
Beneath the empty eyes of the&nbsp;
dead dragons on the walls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.920 --> 00:13:40.320
the last dragon king squealed&nbsp;
like a pig and shat himself.
&nbsp;

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:47.840
So easy, I thought. A king&nbsp;
should die harder than this.

